---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro'
import PageHeader from '../../components/PageHeader.astro'
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro'
import Callout from '../../components/Callout.astro'
import PageLinks from '../../components/PageLinks.astro'
const headings = [
  { depth: 2, slug: 'syntax', text: 'Syntax' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'supported-functions', text: 'Supported functions' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'frames', text: 'Frames' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'nulls-and-offsets', text: 'Nulls and offsets' },
]
---
<DocsLayout title="Window functions" description="Use ranking, value access, and aggregate window functions in thinDB." headings={headings}>
  <PageHeader eyebrow="SQL guide" title="Window functions" description="Compute rankings, running totals, comparisons, and partition-level values without collapsing rows." />
  <h2 id="syntax">Syntax</h2>
  <CodeBlock language="sql" code={`SELECT
  customer_id,
  issued_on,
  amount,
  ROW_NUMBER() OVER (
    PARTITION BY customer_id ORDER BY issued_on, invoice_id
  ) AS invoice_number,
  SUM(amount) OVER (
    PARTITION BY customer_id
    ORDER BY issued_on
    ROWS BETWEEN UNBOUNDED PRECEDING AND CURRENT ROW
  ) AS running_total
FROM invoices;`} />
  <p>Use <code>QUALIFY</code> after the window stage to filter on a window alias without wrapping the query in a subquery.</p>
  <CodeBlock language="sql" code={`SELECT customer_id, invoice_id,
  ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY customer_id ORDER BY issued_on DESC) AS recency
FROM invoices
QUALIFY recency = 1;`} />

  <h2 id="supported-functions">Supported functions</h2>
  <div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Family</th><th>Functions</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td>Ranking</td><td><code>row_number</code>, <code>rank</code>, <code>dense_rank</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td>Value access</td><td><code>lag</code>, <code>lead</code>, <code>first_value</code>, <code>last_value</code>, <code>nth_value</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td>Aggregate windows</td><td><code>sum</code>, <code>avg</code>, <code>count</code>, <code>min</code>, <code>max</code></td></tr>
  </tbody></table></div>
  <Callout type="warning" title="Reserved, not shipped"><p><code>ntile</code>, <code>cume_dist</code>, and <code>percent_rank</code> have reserved parser identities but are rejected by the execution layer. Do not depend on them yet.</p></Callout>

  <h2 id="frames">Frames</h2>
  <p><code>ROWS</code>, <code>RANGE</code>, and <code>GROUPS</code> frame kinds are represented. Bounds include unbounded preceding/following, current row, and supported offset bounds. Without <code>ORDER BY</code>, the default covers the whole partition. With ordering, the default is equivalent to <code>RANGE BETWEEN UNBOUNDED PRECEDING AND CURRENT ROW</code>.</p>
  <CodeBlock language="sql" code={`AVG(amount) OVER (
  PARTITION BY customer_id
  ORDER BY issued_on
  ROWS BETWEEN 2 PRECEDING AND CURRENT ROW
)`} />

  <h2 id="nulls-and-offsets">Nulls and offsets</h2>
  <p><code>LAG</code> and <code>LEAD</code> accept an expression, optional offset, and optional default. Value functions support <code>IGNORE NULLS</code> where meaningful; the default is <code>RESPECT NULLS</code>.</p>
  <CodeBlock language="sql" code={`SELECT
  invoice_id,
  LAG(amount, 1, 0) OVER (PARTITION BY customer_id ORDER BY issued_on) AS prior_amount,
  FIRST_VALUE(memo) IGNORE NULLS OVER (PARTITION BY customer_id ORDER BY issued_on) AS first_memo
FROM invoices;`} />
  <PageLinks previous={{ label: 'Joins', href: '/sql/joins/' }} next={{ label: 'Built-in functions', href: '/sql/functions/' }} />
</DocsLayout>
